# Workflow

Every route starts with steps 1 to 3. The dossier, plan, proof of funds and settle-in workflow files give steps 4 and 5; the updates, library and proof of funds files give their own commands. Each step passes only the real result returned by the previous step; never pass a guessed path or value.

The expert agents see only the instruction, not this conversation. Each command below has slots in square brackets and capitals, such as [DOCUMENTS FOLDER]. Replace every slot with the real folder or the real file paths returned earlier, comma-separated, before running the command; never send a command with a slot left in. Pass file paths, never document numbers, machine readable zone lines or account numbers, and keep every instruction on one line without angle brackets.

Step 1. Find travel documents in the documents folder: the file-agent command in First move.

Step 2. If photo search is yes, find photos of documents in the photo library.

```text
delegate --target photo-agent --instruction 'Search the photo library for pictures classified as cards or documents, and for pictures whose recognised text contains PASSPORT, PASSEPORT, VISA, RESIDENCE PERMIT, BANK STATEMENT or a machine readable zone line starting with P followed by a less-than sign. Return each match with its real file path and date taken. Do not create albums or change anything. If nothing matches, return an empty list and say so.'
```

If steps 1 and 2 both return empty lists, tell the user no documents were found in the folder and photo library they named, and stop. Do not search other folders.

Step 3. Read each travel document found. For PDF files:

```text
delegate --target document-agent --instruction 'From each of these passport, visa, residence permit or national ID files: [PDF PATHS FROM STEP 1], extract one record per document with these fields: document type, issuing country, holder surname, given names, nationality, date of birth, sex, place of birth, the last three characters of the document number, date of issue, date of expiry, issuing authority, and for visas the visa type, entries allowed, duration of stay and valid-from date. Compare the machine readable zone with the printed fields yourself and do not return the machine readable zone lines: say for each document whether the name, document number, date of birth, nationality and expiry in the zone agree with the printed page, and for each field that differs, which character positions differ and the two characters at each. Return a field as empty when it is not visible; never guess. Report each file you could not read.'
```

For image files:

```text
delegate --target photo-agent --instruction 'Run text recognition on each of these images: [IMAGE PATHS FROM STEPS 1 AND 2], and return the full recognised text for each image, keeping the two or three machine readable zone lines at the bottom intact and in order. Report each image where no text was recognised.'
```

Then compare the records for each person yourself, without another delegation: group them by holder, check that surname, given names, date of birth and nationality agree across every document of the same holder, and for images check the machine readable zone against the printed fields using [topics/document-fields.md](references/topics/document-fields.md). Text recognition returns full numbers: use them only for that check, and in the answer write each number as "ending" plus its last three characters. List every disagreement with both values and the file paths involved.

Then follow the workflow file for the chosen route. To save a report or tag files, after the user agrees, read [save.md](references/save.md).

